    "labelChirho": "Magi / wise men from the East",
    "descriptionChirho": "Learned men, probably astrologer-priests from Persia or Babylon, who came to worship the infant Jesus (Matt 2). This is the specialized NT sense of Magos as a reverential title for Eastern sages. Translations reflect this: eng 'magi,' spa 'magos' (wise men), hin jyotishi (ज्योतिषी, astrologers), arb al-majus (الْمَجُوسِ, Zoroastrian wise men), kor baksa (박사, scholars/doctors), swa 'mamajusi' (Magi). The plural and genitive forms all denote the same group.",
