  {
    "labelChirho": "magician / sorcerer",
    "descriptionChirho": "A practitioner of magic arts or sorcery, used pejoratively for figures like Bar-Jesus/Elymas (Acts 13:6,8). This sense is distinct from the reverential 'Magi' usage, carrying connotations of deception and false spiritual power. Multilingual evidence diverges sharply from sense 1: eng 'magician,' spa 'mago' (magician/sorcerer), hin jadugar (जादूगर, sorcerer), arb sahir (ساحِر, sorcerer -- completely different root from majus), kor mabeobsa (마법사, magician), swa 'mchawi' (witch/sorcerer).",
